   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<br>I am running the following code and though its plotting, the plot appears to have been mapped from covariates rather than data.<br>In which way can I improve my mapped plot.<br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\">print(levelplot(row.values=proj.grid$x,column.values=proj.grid$y,\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">x=pred.mean1,\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">col.regions&lt;-tim.colors(64),\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">xlim=c(0.1707613,15.9874216),ylim=c(11.70414,23.52080),\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">aspect=&quot;iso&quot;,\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">xlab=&quot;Easting&quot;,ylab=&quot;Northing&quot;))\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In levelplot.matrix(row.values = proj.grid$x, column.values = proj.grid$y,  :\r\n  explicit &#39;data&#39; specification ignored</span></pre></span>Thanks<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "y-nSavVj1OkJ",
   "from": "Elias T Krainski",
   "author": "66ed4f72a898a51c",
   "date": "2013-12-17T16:07:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Error when plotting predicted mean",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    This is not an error in fact. The message says that you specify the\r\n    data but it is not used. To understand it, is necessary to\r\n    understand how R works with &#39;=&#39; and &#39;&lt;-&#39; to. <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    Your code: <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <br>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\">\r\n        <pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\">print(levelplot(row.values=proj.grid$x,column.values=proj.grid$y,\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">x=pred.mean1,\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">col.regions&lt;-tim.colors(64),\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">xlim=c(0.1707613,15.9874216),ylim=c(11.70414,23.52080),\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">aspect=&quot;iso&quot;,\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">xlab=&quot;Easting&quot;,ylab=&quot;Northing&quot;))</span></pre>\r\n      </span></blockquote>\r\n    <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    one can says &quot;There is no specification of the &#39;data&#39; argument!&quot;\r\n    But, in fact yes!<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    When you do <br>\r\n     levelplot(..., col.regions &lt;- a,  )<br>\r\n    by using &#39;&lt;-&#39; inside the () on a function call, you aren&#39;t\r\n    passing &#39;a&#39; for &#39;col.regions&#39; argument. Because you specify the\r\n    first argument, &#39;x&#39;, explicitely, &#39;a&#39; is assumed as the value for\r\n    &#39;data&#39;, the second argument. It is assigned to &#39;data&#39; because it is\r\n    the first unspecified argument. <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
